node_modules/
dist/
.astro/

# Inspection output from scripts/shoot.sh: 22 full-page captures, 2.3 MB, and
# regenerable in one command against any build. Same reasoning as dist/. They are
# for looking at while changing the page, not a record of it.
screenshots/

# Copies, not sources. `npm run assets` writes every one of these out of the
# repository and records what it came from in assets.lock.json, so committing
# them would be committing the same 20 MB twice.
#
# The exception is the caption track, which is hand-authored against the
# narration script and cannot be regenerated. Git cannot re-include a file whose
# directory is excluded, so public/media is excluded per-entry rather than
# wholesale.
#
# The negation below must name the file that is actually on disk. It read
# `pulse-promo.en.vtt` from the rename in 3.0.0 until 2026-08-10, which matched
# nothing, so the one irreplaceable file in this directory was silently ignored
# by every `git add` for two releases. If the media filenames ever change again,
# this line changes with them.
public/media/*
!public/media/nightbell-promo.en.vtt

# Still copies, and still regenerated by `npm run assets` from things that are
# in the repository: the icons from the app's own mark, the screenshots from
# docs/screens, the videos from docs/video.
public/icon-*.png
public/apple-touch-icon.png
src/assets/screens/

# public/favicon.svg used to be listed above and is deliberately not any more.
# It is no longer a plate flag on the launcher drawing: a tab is not a launcher,
# so the favicon is transparent, full bleed and brand blue, and it ships with a
# .ico because Safari and iOS support no SVG favicon at all. Both are written by
# docs/brand/web_favicon.py, which needs python, shapely, rsvg-convert and
# ImageMagick. Requiring that on a machine that only wants to build the site is
# a worse trade than committing 3.5 KB, so they are committed.
#
# Leaving favicon.svg ignored while favicon.ico was not would have been the worst
# of both: a `git add` would take the .ico and silently drop the .svg, and the
# deployed pair would disagree about what the icon is.

# Committed, not ignored, because their source is not in the repository.
#
# The two faces were lifted out of promo-video/node_modules and the chapter table
# was parsed out of promo-video/src, and promo-video/ is not committed: it is
# 52 MB of Remotion project and intermediate audio to produce one mp4 that is
# committed on its own. 96 KB of derived files here is the cheaper half of that
# trade, and it is the half the site cannot build without.
#
#   public/fonts/
#   src/media.json
